\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Mechanics of Algorithm~\ref {alg:static-scoping} (Static Scoping) on a batch controller pattern. (a)~Java source illustrating recurrent state, mutual recursion, asynchronous concurrency, and transitive $\langle \text  {clinit}\rangle $ triggers. (b)~Augmented call DAG $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle G$}\mathaccent "0365{G}_{\text  {scc}}$ condensing recursive SCCs, severing asynchronous thread edges to $\text  {SUPER\_ROOT}$, and identifying accessor sets $\mathcal  {C}(F)$. (c)~Immediate dominator tree $\text  {idom}_{\text  {scc}}$ resolving capturing methods: $F_{\text  {met}}$ collapses to \text  {GLOBAL}{}, $F_{\text  {def}}$ is bound to $C_{\text  {batch}}$ via $\langle \text  {clinit}\rangle $ attribution, and $F_{\text  {cache}}$ is lifted from $C_{\text  {fmt}}$ to $C_{\text  {batch}}$ via Theorem~\ref {thm:reentrancy}.}}{14}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dgss-comprehensive}{{4}{14}{Mechanics of Algorithm~\ref {alg:static-scoping} (Static Scoping) on a batch controller pattern. (a)~Java source illustrating recurrent state, mutual recursion, asynchronous concurrency, and transitive $\langle \text {clinit}\rangle $ triggers. (b)~Augmented call DAG $\widetilde {G}_{\text {scc}}$ condensing recursive SCCs, severing asynchronous thread edges to $\text {SUPER\_ROOT}$, and identifying accessor sets $\mathcal {C}(F)$. (c)~Immediate dominator tree $\idom _{\text {scc}}$ resolving capturing methods: $F_{\text {met}}$ collapses to \GLOBAL {}, $F_{\text {def}}$ is bound to $C_{\text {batch}}$ via $\langle \text {clinit}\rangle $ attribution, and $F_{\text {cache}}$ is lifted from $C_{\text {fmt}}$ to $C_{\text {batch}}$ via Theorem~\ref {thm:reentrancy}}{figure.caption.8}{}}
